      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "This retrospective analysis of clinical data for children (2-18 years old) with incident T1D found surprisingly low (9%) prevalence of underweight, and high (15% overweight; 8% obesity) respectively at diagnosis. These results suggests a need to rethink the classic clinical teaching surrounding skinnier presentation at diagnosis, and importantly, the corresponding expectation of weight gain after insulin therapy initiation."
      },
